+>
+> The earlier `28 failed` was a **configuration** gap, not a code defect — I said "pre-existing
+> bug in `setup.ts`" before, and that was wrong. `setup.ts` only acquires a Bearer token when
+> `E2E_REMOTE` is false; with the Basic-auth configuration below it is skipped entirely. Nothing
+> in `src/` needs changing.
+>
+> Three environment variables are required, beyond the `LOCAL_BASIC_AUTH_*` block:
+>
+> | Variable | Value | Why |
+> | --- | --- | --- |
+> | `E2E_REMOTE` | `true` | Makes the e2e client send **Basic**. Despite the name this flag means "Basic-auth caller" in `role-assignments.test.ts` — see the note below. |
+> | `E2E_BASIC_AUTH_TOKEN` | any base64, e.g. `$(printf 'e2e:e2e' \| base64)` | With `LOCAL_BASIC_AUTH_*` set, `authMiddleware` trusts **any** Basic header and maps it to that identity without calling the auth Lambda, so the value is arbitrary locally. |
+> | `E2E_ACCOUNT_ID` | must equal `LOCAL_BASIC_AUTH_ACCOUNT_ID` (`1501`) | Otherwise `assertAuthMatchesRequest` 403s every scoped request. |
+>
+> `E2E_ORG_ID` must also match `LOCAL_BASIC_AUTH_ORGANIZATION_ID`, and that org must be one
+> `dev.ts` seeds system roles for (`00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002`). Pointing the Basic
+> identity at an unseeded org leaves `roles.test.ts` failing 5 tests on missing system roles —
+> that was the only remaining failure before the org was aligned. Both already default correctly
+> in `src/e2e/config.ts`.
+>
+> **Naming wart worth a separate cleanup:** `E2E_REMOTE` is doing double duty. The comment at
+> `role-assignments.test.ts:218` ("Basic auth service callerType has no assignments to enforce
+> against") and the three `if (E2E_REMOTE) return;` early-returns in the legacy-fallback tests are
+> all really about *Basic vs Bearer*, not *local vs deployed*. A dedicated flag would let
+> `test-e2e-local.sh` configure this itself instead of requiring every developer to set
+> `E2E_REMOTE=true` against `localhost`. Out of scope here; worth a note in
+> `agent_docs/development-workflow.md`.
