+### Coverage matrix
+
+Six fixture users, one role, all in `sandbox`. Every query point gets its own assertion of who is in and who is out, because the winner a user resolves to depends on the query point.
+
+| Fixture | Grant | @ account | @ account+site | @ account+site+store |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `accountUser` | account | **in** (account) | **in** (account) | **in** (account) |
+| `siteUser` | site `S` | out (deeper) | **in** (site) | **in** (site) |
+| `storeUser` | stores `[ST, ST+1, ST+2]` in `S` | out (deeper) | out (deeper) | **in** (store, full fan-out) |
+| `bothUser` | site `S` **and** store `[ST]` | out (deeper) | **in** (site wins) | **in** (store wins) |
+| `otherSiteUser` | site `S+500` | out (deeper) | out (wrong site) | out (wrong site) |
+| `otherStoreUser` | store `[ST+900]` in `S` | out (deeper) | out (deeper) | out (wrong store) |
+
+`bothUser` is the load-bearing fixture: the same user resolves to a different winning assignment at each query point. `otherStoreUser` is what distinguishes "wrong store, right site" from "deeper than the query point".
